## Timer Management

### Rules
- Wrap `setTimeout`/`setInterval` in a `TimerManager` or track IDs in an array for cleanup.
- Prefer GSAP's `gsap.delayedCall(seconds, callback)` over raw `setTimeout` — GSAP delayed calls are automatically killed by `gsap.killTweensOf()` and can be paused/resumed.
- Never use `setTimeout` for animation sequencing. Use GSAP timelines with `.add()` and proper `position` parameters.

```ts
// BAD — fragile timing chain that can't be cancelled
setTimeout(() => {
  this.animatePhaseTwo();
  setTimeout(() => {
    this.startTurn();
  }, 1500);
}, 2000);

// GOOD — cancellable GSAP timeline
const timeline = gsap.timeline();
timeline.call(() => this.animatePhaseTwo(), null, "+=2");
timeline.call(() => this.startTurn(), null, "+=1.5");
// On destroy: timeline.kill();
```

