## Guard Against Destroyed Objects

Before operating on a PixiJS display object in an async callback (timer, tween `onComplete`, promise `.then`), check if the object is still alive:

```ts
gsap.to(this.card, {
  x: 100,
  duration: 0.5,
  onComplete: () => {
    if (this.destroyed) return; // Guard — screen may have been destroyed mid-animation
    this.card.visible = false;
  },
});
```

This prevents silent errors when a screen is destroyed while animations are in flight.

---

## `app.stage` Usage

- Never add sprites or containers directly to `app.stage` outside of the top-level screen management (Navigation class).
- `eventListeners.ts` must not create display objects on `app.stage`. If an overlay is needed, route through the Navigation popup system.
